#%PAM-1.0
# The AUTOLOGIN stack, named by `[initial_session] service =` in greetd's config.
#
# greetd starts the initial session UNAUTHENTICATED - `worker.rs` runs
# `pam.authenticate()` only when its `authenticate` flag is set, and the initial
# session goes through `start_unauthenticated_session` - so the auth stack below is
# never consulted for it. It permits anyway, because a stack that is never reached
# should not be the thing that decides whether the machine boots.
#
# It used to be called `greetd`, which is ALSO the service a real password login
# uses. That was harmless while nothing could type a password and became a lie the
# moment the greeter shipped: one permissive file would have opened the machine to
# any password at all. Splitting it is what lets `/etc/pam.d/greetd` be strict
# without touching the boot path.
#
# The session stack is what matters here - it must register a logind session
# (pam_systemd) so XDG_RUNTIME_DIR / XDG_SEAT / XDG_VTNR exist for the compositor
# + libseat. Self-contained (no @include common-*) so it works in the minimal image
# regardless of pam-auth-update state.
auth       required pam_permit.so
account    required pam_permit.so
password   required pam_permit.so
session    optional pam_keyinit.so force revoke
session    required pam_loginuid.so
session    required pam_permit.so
session    optional pam_systemd.so
